        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">LIVESTRONG treadmills were built by Johnson Health Tech under a
          licence that began in 2009, and they are no longer sold new in the US.</strong> The LS10.0T
          is confirmed at a 325 lb user limit with a lifetime frame and motor warranty when new, and
          its parts are better catalogued than most discontinued treadmills — though the incline
          motor and speed sensor are no longer listed.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep a working one lubricated and running, buy a used one only cheaply and after seeing it
